<Layouts.app flash={@flash} active={:districts} prompt={false}>
  <section id="find-page" class="editorial-shell bg-[var(--paper)]">
    <header class="section-pad border-b-2 border-[var(--ink)]">
      <p class="eyebrow">Find your seat</p>

      <h1 :if={@state == :prompt} class="display-lg mt-7 max-w-4xl">
        Which district are you in?
      </h1>
      <h1 :if={@state == :choose} class="display-lg mt-7 max-w-4xl">
        {String.upcase(@zip)} is in {length(@matches)} districts.
      </h1>
      <h1 :if={@state == :malformed} class="display-lg mt-7 max-w-4xl">
        That isn't a ZIP code.
      </h1>
      <h1 :if={@state == :unknown} class="display-lg mt-7 max-w-4xl">
        The Census has no area for {@zip}.
      </h1>
      <h1 :if={@state == :no_district} class="display-lg mt-7 max-w-4xl">
        {@zip} has no vote to withhold.
      </h1>

      <form action={~p"/find"} method="get" class="find-form mt-10">
        <label for="find-zip" class="data-label">Your ZIP code</label>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-stretch gap-4">
          <input
            type="text"
            id="find-zip"
            name="zip"
            value={@state in [:choose] && @zip}
            inputmode="numeric"
            autocomplete="postal-code"
            maxlength="10"
            placeholder="43604"
            class="w-44 border-2 border-[var(--ink)] bg-[var(--paper-bright)] p-4 font-mono text-2xl font-bold tracking-widest"
          />
          <button type="submit" class="ink-button">
            Find the seat <span>→</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </form>

      <p :if={@state == :prompt} class="mt-9 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6">
        We work this out from published geometry rather than a bought lookup table: Census ZIP Code
        Tabulation Areas intersected with the district lines in force, by our own method.
        <.link navigate={~p"/methodology#methodology-zip"} class="underline">
          How the crosswalk works
        </.link>
      </p>

      <p :if={@state == :malformed} class="mt-9 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6">
        Five digits. We take ZIP+4 too and use the first five.
      </p>

      <p :if={@state == :unknown} class="mt-9 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6">
        Not every ZIP has a Census area. USPS ZIPs that serve only PO boxes or a single large
        building cover no ground, so the Census draws no polygon for them and we have nothing to
        intersect. Try the ZIP where you sleep, not where you collect mail.
      </p>

      <div :if={@state == :no_district} class="mt-9 max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm leading-6">
          That area is real and its people are represented — by a delegate who cannot vote on
          final passage. Washington DC and the territories elect one, and this site measures the
          435 seats that decide legislation. There is no incumbent here for you to vote against,
          which is its own argument and not one we are making today.
        </p>
        <.link navigate={~p"/districts"} class="ink-button mt-8">
          Open the directory <span>→</span>
        </.link>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div :if={@state == :choose}>
      <div class="section-pad border-b-2 border-[var(--ink)] bg-[var(--yellow)]">
        <p class="max-w-3xl font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">
          A ZIP code is a mail route, not a district. Yours is split, so we will not choose for
          you — look at the shapes and pick the one you live in.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6">
          The share is how much of the ZIP's <em>area</em>
          sits in each district. It is not how many people, and the biggest slice is not
          necessarily yours.
        </p>
      </div>

      <%!-- Columns follow the count so an odd row never leaves a bordered
      hole: two and four fill a 2-up, three fills a 3-up. --%>
      <div
        id="find-choices"
        class={[
          "grid md:grid-cols-2",
          length(@matches) == 3 && "lg:grid-cols-3"
        ]}
      >
        <.link
          :for={district <- @matches}
          navigate={~p"/districts/#{district.slug}?from=zip"}
          id={"find-choice-#{district.slug}"}
          class="find-choice section-pad !py-10 border-b-2 border-[var(--ink)] md:border-r-2"
        >
          <span class="data-label">{district.share_label} of the ZIP</span>

          <.district_shape
            path={district.shape_path}
            tone={district.tone}
            class="mt-8 h-44 w-full text-[var(--ink)]"
          />

          <h2 class="display-md mt-9">{district.label}</h2>
          <p :if={district.incumbent_name} class="mt-5 font-serif text-xl leading-tight">
            {district.incumbent_name}
            <span :if={district.incumbent_party}>({district.incumbent_party})</span>
          </p>
          <p :if={district.incumbent_since} class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6">
            Holding this seat since {district.incumbent_since}.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-7 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">
            Open this district <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </p>
        </.link>
      </div>

      <div class="section-pad">
        <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6">
          Not sure which is yours? The county and place lines on each district page name what it
          covers.
          <.link navigate={~p"/methodology#methodology-zip"} class="underline">
            How this crosswalk is computed
          </.link>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
